Subject: [PATCH] feat(evening-card): the evening hour is the person's own
 setting (frontend 06:30Z item 6)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The frontend's 06:30Z list (Misho, the new design), item 6: the
notifications block sets the evening card's hour. Until now it was fixed at
19:00 (#1850).

- Migration 232: "User".evening_card_hour, nullable, 8 to 22. NULL keeps
  19:00.
- GET /evening-card/hour → { hour }; PUT /evening-card/hour { hour: 8..22 |
  null } → { hour }. 400 for anything else.
- The card a question goes on is made for the person's own hour. A card
  already made for today keeps its time, so the new hour applies from the
  next card on.
- The bounds keep the card's one push out of the quiet hours.

DONE WHEN: a person who sets 21 gets the next card at 21:00 their time;
null brings back 19:00; 3 or 19.5 are refused.

